WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
师傅说“对着红标推”。新人却把滑块卡住了。
“Push toward the red mark,” says the instructor. The learner jams the slider.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.000
你第一反应会怎么解释？
What is your first explanation?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
师傅从这一侧看，红标就在挡板前面。
From the instructor’s side, the red mark is in front of the shield.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.400
转到新人这边。红标被挡住了。
Turn to the learner’s side. The red mark is hidden.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.000
同一次失误，有了一个新的解释。
The same jam now has another possible explanation.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.600
从一次行为推断原因，叫归因。先把能看到的事实和猜测分开。
Attribution is explaining behavior. Separate what you observed from your guess.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.000
“滑块卡住了”是观察，“他不用心”还需要证据。
The jam was observed. Carelessness remains a hypothesis.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.100
知道红标的人，很难想象第一次看不到它的人怎么理解。
Knowing the mark makes it hard to imagine a first-timer’s view.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.000
把自己的知识当作共同知识，就是知识诅咒的一种表现。
Treating your knowledge as shared illustrates the curse of knowledge.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.500
先问他看到了什么，再复述一遍自己的理解。
Ask what the learner saw, then paraphrase what you heard.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:51.000
“你只看见两个槽，所以选了离手近的那个？”
“You could only see two slots, so you picked the nearer one?”

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.300
补上共同参照。“黄点朝上，推到第一道刻线。”
Give a shared reference. “Yellow dot up, then push to the first line.”

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:02.000
让对方试一次，确认听到的指令和你想表达的一致。
Have them try it and check that the instruction was understood.
